# Two granularities are wanted, both first-class (ruled 2026-08-28): the
# studio will show the .inkt disassembly beside the source, so an author
# can watch a line and the instructions it became at the same time.
#
# `stepi` is what exists today — VM-instruction stepping with call-depth
# awareness. Line stepping (`step`) is #3264 and is NOT implemented; the
# parser refuses it with a pointer rather than aliasing it here.
#
# This golden therefore records instruction granularity as CORRECT
# behaviour for `stepi`, not as a defect: four instructions happen to make
# up line 7. What #3264 adds is a second verb, so this transcript should
# stay as it is when that lands.
break story.ink:7
run
expect-line 7
stepi over
stepi over
stepi over
stepi over
expect-line 8
locals
expect-local who = "vendor"
stack
